{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Mount Hor and encamped at Zalmonah.</b> — These places, Zalmonah and Punon, were on the way by the Sea of Reeds, around the land of Edom, and the people's spirit grew short on the way. Now they spoke against Elohim and against Moses on the way, and He sent the fiery serpents against them as they traveled on the way and as they encamped in the camp. And Moses made a serpent of bronze, and they would carry it before the standard throughout the entire journey and during their encampments at Zalmonah and at Punon, and it did not depart from them until they encamped at Oboth. Therefore Scripture did not mention a place-name for that event, but said there: \"And the children of Israel journeyed and encamped at Oboth\" (Numbers 21:10), and did not say \"And they journeyed from such-and-such a place and encamped at Oboth,\" as it says for all the journeys — for throughout this entire route the matter was ongoing, from when they journeyed from Mount Hor until they encamped at Oboth. And they journeyed from Oboth and encamped at Iye-abarim, and from there they journeyed and encamped at Dibon-gad and at Almon-diblathaim and the Abarim — and these are places in the wadi Zered:"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:09.696136630Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}